## 5. PostgreSQL checkpoint and outbox implementation

Reuse the previous `Checkpoint` and `OutgoingRecord` records:

```java
public record Checkpoint(
        int version,
        String sourceId,
        String fileName,
        String sha256,
        long nextRecord,
        boolean completed
) {}

public record OutgoingRecord(String key, String json) {}
```

Replace `KafkaJournal` with the following Spring-managed component.

The database transaction locks the checkpoint row, verifies that the batch starts at the current position, inserts the events, and advances the checkpoint. PostgreSQL’s `FOR UPDATE` lock serializes competing updates to the same checkpoint. ([postgresql.org](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/17/explicit-locking.html?utm_source=openai))

### `PostgresJournal.java`

```java
package com.example.ingest;

import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.SQLException;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.Base64;
import java.util.List;

import javax.sql.DataSource;

import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Value;
import org.springframework.jdbc.core.JdbcTemplate;
import org.springframework.jdbc.support.JdbcTransactionManager;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;
import org.springframework.transaction.TransactionDefinition;
import org.springframework.transaction.support.TransactionTemplate;

@Component
public class PostgresJournal {

    private final JdbcTemplate jdbc;
    private final TransactionTemplate transaction;
    private final String sourceId;

    public PostgresJournal(
            DataSource dataSource,
            @Value("${ingest.source-id}") String sourceId
    ) {
        this.jdbc = new JdbcTemplate(dataSource);
        this.sourceId = sourceId;

        // Explicitly a JDBC transaction manager, not a Kafka manager.
        this.transaction = new TransactionTemplate(
                new JdbcTransactionManager(dataSource)
        );

        this.transaction.setIsolationLevel(
                TransactionDefinition.ISOLATION_READ_COMMITTED
        );
        this.transaction.setTimeout(30);
    }

    public Checkpoint checkpoint(String fileName) {
        List<Checkpoint> results = jdbc.query("""
                SELECT source_id, file_name, sha256,
                       next_record, completed
                FROM csv_checkpoint
                WHERE source_id = ? AND file_name = ?
                """,
                PostgresJournal::mapCheckpoint,
                sourceId,
                fileName
        );

        return results.isEmpty() ? null : results.getFirst();
    }

    public List<Checkpoint> checkpoints() {
        return jdbc.query("""
                SELECT source_id, file_name, sha256,
                       next_record, completed
                FROM csv_checkpoint
                WHERE source_id = ?
                """,
                PostgresJournal::mapCheckpoint,
                sourceId
        );
    }

    public void commit(
            List<OutgoingRecord> records,
            Checkpoint next
    ) {
        // Defensive copy: caller must not change the batch during commit.
        List<OutgoingRecord> batch = List.copyOf(records);

        if (next.version() != 1
                || !sourceId.equals(next.sourceId())
                || next.nextRecord() < batch.size()
                || next.sha256() == null
                || !next.sha256().matches("[0-9a-f]{64}")) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid checkpoint");
        }

        if (batch.isEmpty() && !next.completed()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                    "An empty batch must complete the file"
            );
        }

        long expectedPosition = next.nextRecord() - batch.size();

        String fileId = sourceId + ":" +
                Base64.getUrlEncoder()
                        .withoutPadding()
                        .encodeToString(
                                next.fileName().getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8)
                        );

        // Prepare parameters before acquiring database locks.
        List<Object[]> inserts = new ArrayList<>(batch.size());

        for (int i = 0; i < batch.size(); i++) {
            long recordIndex = expectedPosition + i;
            String eventId = fileId + ":" + recordIndex;

            OutgoingRecord record = batch.get(i);

            if (!eventId.equals(record.key())) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                        "Unexpected event ID at record " + recordIndex
                );
            }

            inserts.add(new Object[] {
                    eventId,
                    "csv",
                    fileId,
                    "CsvRecord",
                    record.json(),
                    sourceId,
                    next.fileName(),
                    recordIndex
            });
        }

        transaction.executeWithoutResult(status -> {
            jdbc.update("""
                    INSERT INTO csv_checkpoint (
                        source_id, file_name, sha256,
                        next_record, completed
                    )
                    VALUES (?, ?, ?, 0, false)
                    ON CONFLICT (source_id, file_name) DO NOTHING
                    """,
                    sourceId,
                    next.fileName(),
                    next.sha256()
            );

            Checkpoint current = jdbc.queryForObject("""
                    SELECT source_id, file_name, sha256,
                           next_record, completed
                    FROM csv_checkpoint
                    WHERE source_id = ? AND file_name = ?
                    FOR UPDATE
                    """,
                    PostgresJournal::mapCheckpoint,
                    sourceId,
                    next.fileName()
            );

            if (current == null) {
                throw new IllegalStateException("Checkpoint missing");
            }

            if (!current.sha256().equals(next.sha256())) {
                throw new IllegalStateException(
                        "Source file changed: " + next.fileName()
                );
            }

            if (current.completed()
                    || current.nextRecord() != expectedPosition) {
                throw new IllegalStateException(
                        "Stale batch for " + next.fileName()
                        + "; reload its checkpoint before continuing"
                );
            }

            if (!inserts.isEmpty()) {
                jdbc.batchUpdate("""
                        INSERT INTO ingest_outbox (
                            id, aggregatetype, aggregateid, type,
                            payload, source_id, file_name, record_index
                        )
                        VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, CAST(? AS jsonb), ?, ?, ?)
                        """,
                        inserts
                );
            }

            int updated = jdbc.update("""
                    UPDATE csv_checkpoint
                    SET next_record = ?,
                        completed = ?,
                        updated_at = now()
                    WHERE source_id = ?
                      AND file_name = ?
                      AND next_record = ?
                      AND completed = false
                    """,
                    next.nextRecord(),
                    next.completed(),
                    sourceId,
                    next.fileName(),
                    expectedPosition
            );

            if (updated != 1) {
                throw new IllegalStateException(
                        "Checkpoint update failed"
                );
            }
        });

        // Return only after the PostgreSQL transaction commits.
    }

    private static Checkpoint mapCheckpoint(
            ResultSet rs,
            int rowNumber
    ) throws SQLException {
        return new Checkpoint(
                1,
                rs.getString("source_id"),
                rs.getString("file_name"),
                rs.getString("sha256"),
                rs.getLong("next_record"),
                rs.getBoolean("completed")
        );
    }
}
```

`TransactionTemplate` explicitly controls the transaction boundary, without depending on an internally called `@Transactional` method being intercepted by a Spring proxy. It is Spring’s recommended imperative programmatic transaction API. ([docs.spring.io](https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/reference/data-access/transaction/programmatic.html))

### Why no `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` for outbox inserts?

In this design, a duplicate outbox event is an invariant violation. It should roll back the batch rather than be silently ignored.

After an uncertain database commit, **reload the checkpoint before reading another batch**. Do not blindly retry using the same in-memory position.

