## 7. Publishing the outbox with Debezium

For your original exactly-once requirement, deploy Debezium as a **Kafka Connect source connector with source EOS enabled**.

On every worker in a **new distributed Connect cluster**:

```properties
exactly.once.source.support=enabled
```

For an existing cluster, Kafka documents a staged `preparing` → `enabled` rollout rather than changing only one worker. ([kafka.apache.org](https://kafka.apache.org/41/configuration/kafka-connect-configs/))

The following is a connector configuration template; secrets, TLS trust, ACLs, and infrastructure provisioning must be supplied by your deployment.

```json
{
  "name": "csv-outbox",
  "config": {
    "connector.class": "io.debezium.connector.postgresql.PostgresConnector",
    "tasks.max": "1",

    "database.hostname": "postgres.example.internal",
    "database.port": "5432",
    "database.user": "csv_cdc",
    "database.password": "<inject-secret>",
    "database.dbname": "ingestion",
    "database.sslmode": "verify-full",

    "topic.prefix": "csv_ingestion",
    "plugin.name": "pgoutput",

    "slot.name": "csv_outbox_slot",
    "publication.name": "csv_outbox_publication",
    "publication.autocreate.mode": "disabled",

    "table.include.list": "public.ingest_outbox",
    "snapshot.mode": "initial",

    "exactly.once.support": "required",
    "transaction.boundary": "poll",

    "transforms": "outbox",
    "transforms.outbox.type": "io.debezium.transforms.outbox.EventRouter",
    "transforms.outbox.route.topic.replacement": "csv.events",
    "transforms.outbox.table.expand.json.payload": "true",
    "transforms.outbox.table.op.invalid.behavior": "fatal",

    "key.converter": "org.apache.kafka.connect.storage.StringConverter",
    "value.converter": "org.apache.kafka.connect.json.JsonConverter",
    "value.converter.schemas.enable": "false",

    "errors.tolerance": "none"
  }
}
```

The outbox router uses `aggregateid` as the Kafka key and `payload` as the value. JSON expansion prevents publishing the JSON document as an escaped JSON string. Here, the file ID is the key, keeping records from a file on the same partition while the partition count remains unchanged. ([debezium.io](https://debezium.io/documentation/reference/stable/transformations/outbox-event-router.html))

Provision the publication with an appropriately privileged database role:

```sql
CREATE PUBLICATION csv_outbox_publication
FOR TABLE public.ingest_outbox;
```

PostgreSQL must be configured for logical replication, with an appropriately permissioned CDC user and replication slot capacity. Monitor replication-slot WAL retention, especially while the connector is unavailable. ([debezium.io](https://debezium.io/documentation/reference/stable/connectors/postgresql.html))

Consumers of `csv.events` must use:

```properties
isolation.level=read_committed
```

Source EOS makes Kafka Connect commit source records and source offsets transactionally; downstream consumers must respect those transaction boundaries. ([debezium.io](https://debezium.io/documentation/reference/stable/configuration/eos.html))

